\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The Gaussian convention fixes the interaction}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{The [continuum half-Dirichlet law](fdip-00I2) uses covariance
#{(-\Delta_{\Lambda,D}+m_0^2I)^{-1}} with characteristic exponent
#{-\langle f,Cf\rangle /2}. Its polynomial is #{P(u)=\lambda u^4/24},
its external field is zero, and its Wick ordering uses the free
whole-space covariance at the same mass. These are precisely
\citet{(3.9)-(3.10), p. 275; (3.79)-(3.81), pp. 293-294}{frohlich1974schwingerI}.
Taking the closure of an open square preserves its Dirichlet interior
and changes the interaction on a set of area zero.}

\p{The factor #{1/2} agrees with
\citet{(IV.3)-(IV.9)}{guerra1975euclideanII}.
The Gaussian displays (3.2), (3.10) and (3.11) of
\citek{frohlich1974verification} print incompatible exponents.
The continuum law here is supplied directly by
\citek{frohlich1974schwingerI}; the abstract reconstruction theorem
and the nonfreeness result from the other paper apply to this law
through their stated hypotheses and named source construction.}
